{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A retry that fails before the next poll can leave subsequent owner approvals rejected indefinitely, while same-second failures can also reuse an earlier approval."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A precisely aligned set of persistent failures can indefinitely prevent a healthy issue's lifecycle update from being delivered."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The existing suite lacks regression coverage for F1 and F2, with no independent runtime effect."}]}